      <p>Chinese chillies lean toward colour and aromatic varieties with controlled heat (Jinta, Zidantou, Erjingtiao); Indian chillies span the full heat spectrum, from mild Kashmiri to super-hot Bhut Jolokia, and India dominates dried-chilli export.</p>
